A note on what hosting does and does not mean for licensing. This program loads
LV2 and VST3 plug-ins that the user chose and that this project neither ships nor
links. Some of them will be GPL-licensed; that is the user's own act of running
two programs together, and it places no obligation on this source tree. The
converse is equally the user's act: running a proprietary plug-in in the GPLv3
Windows build is loading a plug-in, not conveying a combined work.

What this project enforces on its own include graph is that no dependency arrives
under terms it cannot satisfy. No JUCE header may enter it at all. Every
dependency named below is MIT, BSD, Apache-2.0, MPL-2.0, ISC, zlib or OFL — with
the single exception of the ASIO SDK, taken under GPLv3, Windows-only, and
conditioned in the section that names it.

